# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009240> (formiminoglutamic aciduria)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:51208") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009240> "Formiminoglutamic aciduria, in its moderate form and in the absence of histidine administration, is characterized by mild developmental delay and elevated concentrations of formiminoglutamate (FIGLU) in the urine. A more severe phenotype has been described in five members of a Japanese family and included severe intellectual deficit, psychomotor retardation and megaloblastic anemia.")
