# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009443> (autosomal recessive congenital ichthyosis 4B)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:457") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009443> "Harlequin ichthyosis (HI) is the most severe variant of autosomal recessive congenital ichthyosis (ARCI). It is characterized at birth by the presence of large, thick, plate-like scales over the whole body associated with severe ectropion, eclabium, and flattened ears, that later develops into a severe scaling erythroderma.")
